http_reqs............: 147000  1225.0/s

Statement: "Run B shows that the leaderboard endpoint can serve about three times the load that run A measured, with no errors."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Load served is throughput: completed requests per second. It went from 1210.4/s to 1225.0/s, about 1% more, while the number of requests in flight (the VUs) tripled. With throughput flat at the server''s capacity, the extra concurrency can only turn into waiting time, and it did: 1225.0/s x 0.2446 s = 300 requests in flight, the 300 VUs, and the average latency tripled from 82 ms to 245 ms. The common misconception is to read VUs (concurrency) as capacity: three times the VUs means three times as many requests waiting, not three times as many served.', 1, 5
