Statement: "The database is the first bottleneck: under load each INSERT got slower, the connections stayed busy longer, and the pool ran out. Tuning the INSERT (an index, a faster disk) is the fix."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The INSERT is 5 ms at p50 and 11 ms at p95 in the spike, almost the same as at 160/s, and PostgreSQL CPU is at 31%. The mean hold time of a connection is 38 ms both at 160/s and in the spike, and most of it is the PUT of the source code to object storage, which runs inside the transaction while the connection is held. The database is not slow; the connection is held for work that does not need it. The misconception is that a pool running out means the database is slow.', 4, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_qpr_321') AND order_index = 4)
    RETURNING id
)
